/Title (The author learned how a game loop works, how the position and speed of a character can be changed in every update, and how gravity and jumping can be created with simple arithmetic. Rectangle-based collision detection was used for platforms, coins, enemies and the boss, and it showed how the same idea can solve many different problems. Handling keyboard input with GetAsyncKeyState and window messages was another important part of the work, as was managing game states such as the menu, playing, level complete, game over and win screens.)
/Dest [43 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1459 0 R
/Prev 1922 0 R
/Next 2580 0 R
>>
endobj
2352 0 obj
<<
/Title (The program is a simple game and is written in a structured style with structures and functions. It does not use classes, inheritance or polymorphism, so it should not be seen as a full object-oriented design. The following ideas are possible future improvements and are not part of the present version: converting the structures into classes with member functions, adding collectible power-up items in the levels, adding sound effects, adding more worlds and enemy types, and saving the highest score.)
/Dest [43 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1459 0 R
/Prev 2580 0 R
/Next 1923 0 R
>>
endobj
