/Title (The game is written in C++ and uses the Windows API to create and manage its window. A window procedure receives messages such as key presses, timer ticks and paint requests. A timer fires about every 16 milliseconds, and on each tick the program updates the game and redraws the screen. All pictures in the game are created with Windows GDI functions that draw rectangles, circles and text, so no image files are needed. An off-screen bitmap is used as a back buffer, so each frame is prepared first and then copied to the window in one step.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2578 0 R
/Prev 2800 0 R
/Next 2801 0 R
>>
