/Title (Window creation and start-up. The program starts in WinMain. It registers a window class named MarioAdventureWindow, creates a window titled "Mario Adventure - The Three Worlds" of size 900 by 600 pixels \(with the maximise button removed\), shows it, and then enters the standard message loop. All events are sent to the function WindowProcedure. When the window is created \(WM_CREATE\), the program creates an off-screen drawing buffer and starts a timer of 16 milliseconds. Game loop and game states. Every timer message \(WM_TIMER\) calls UpdateGame, which changes the game data, and then asks Windows to repaint the window. During painting \(WM_PAINT\) the function Paint draws the current screen into the back buffer and BitBlt copies it to the window. The current screen is stored in the variable mode, which is an enumeration of type GameMode with six values:)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2990 0 R
/Next 2996 0 R
>>
endobj
