2998 0 obj
<<
/Title (Lives and checkpoints. The player starts the game with three lives. LoseLife reduces the number of lives by one. If lives remain, the player is placed back at the starting position \(x = 80\) or, if the checkpoint has been reached, at the checkpoint position \(x = 1100\). When the player's x position passes 1050 for the first time in a world, the checkpoint is saved, 50 points are added and the message CHECKPOINT SAVED is displayed. The code also contains a test for falling below the screen, but in the present levels the ground is continuous, so lives are mainly lost by touching enemies or the boss. When the number of lives reaches zero, the game changes to the game-over screen.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2994 0 R
/Next 3002 0 R
>>
